body:
> Looks like this line of code is bailing out of the transition for some reason:

That line is fine. It returns early for POP, because POP transitions change the URL immediately. For PUSH&REPLACE we need to change the URL manually once the transition finishes. The listener callback happens after that.

As far as I can tell the problem is in [useRoutes.listen](https://github.com/rackt/react-router/blob/master/modules/useRoutes.js#L214) . `state` reflects the old location in contrast to what the comment suggests. With transition hooks, `match` doesn't get to [the line](https://github.com/rackt/react-router/blob/master/modules/useRoutes.js#L52) where it updates `state` since it [branches](https://github.com/rackt/react-router/blob/master/modules/useRoutes.js#L42) on `partialNextState`.

My guess is that that branch should update `state` in the `finishMatch` callback as well:

``` js
function match(location, callback) {
  if (partialNextState && partialNextState.location === location) {
    // Continue from where we left off.
    finishMatch(partialNextState, function (err, nextLocation, nextState) {
      if (nextState)
        state = nextState
      callback(err, nextLocation, nextState)
    });
  } else { ... }
}
```

I've found that wrapping the `pushState` call in a timeout seems to fix the problem. I'm not sure why, but so far so good.

```
window.setTimeout(function() {
    this.props.history.pushState(null, '/protected');
}.bind(this), 500);
```
